## Readiness Gate Transfer

1. `G1-EXECUTIVE-CONTRACT-AND-ENTRY` — contract and stable `work/100k.md` entry point.
2. `G2-COMPLETE-ACCOUNTING` — exhaustive ledger and controlled attention/coverage findings.
3. `G3-OPERATOR-SURFACE-CONVERGENCE` — one operator review with existing APIs retained as drill-down.
4. `G4-PARITY-RECOVERY-AND-PORTABILITY` — deterministic, recovery-safe cross-platform Work2 proof.

## Program Shape

Deliver one bounded Work2 candidate. Implement and document the local executive projection, prove
its deterministic refresh and no-skip behavior under file and SQLite authority, update shipped
manifest coverage, deploy the exact commit to configured development web/Linux/Windows targets,
register the complete owner chain, and checkpoint. Do not publish or promote production.

## Constraints And Non-Goals

- No new database, document type, lifecycle engine, queue, hosted write-back, or second project
  projection.
- No migration or mutation of the DisplayTest source without direct access and separate no-loss
  evidence.
- No forced implementation of every idea; explicit deferral, decline, supersession, exclusion, or
  monitoring remains valid accounting.
- No production release, production deployment, or installed-client synchronization at Work2.

## Completion Boundary

This map is complete when all four gates pass and the exact Work2 candidate is registered and
checkpointed after configured development verification. Publication, DisplayTest migration, and
future hosted interaction remain separate outcomes.
